.\" Generated from packages/nvidia/drivers-install.8.in by scripts/render.py. Edit the .in file, not this one.
.TH oaxaca-drivers-install 8 "2026-10-08" "Oaxaca" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
oaxaca-drivers-install \- install the drivers for this machine, with the newest NVIDIA open branch that has prebuilt modules
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oaxaca-drivers-install
.RB [ --show ]
.RI [ ubuntu-drivers-install-options ]
.RI [ driver ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B oaxaca-drivers-install
runs
.B "ubuntu-drivers install --no-oem --package-list /var/log/oaxaca/drivers.list"
as root, after choosing the NVIDIA branch itself.
.B ubuntu-drivers
(from the
.B ubuntu-drivers-common
package) reads the PCI ids of the running machine under /sys, maps them to driver packages through the apt cache, and installs one list with apt. For an NVIDIA GPU it picks Canonical's prebuilt signed kernel modules
.RB ( linux-modules-nvidia-* ),
so Secure Boot needs no MOK enrollment; DKMS modules are considered only with
.BR --include-dkms .
.PP
Left to itself,
.B ubuntu-drivers
installs the branch it marks "recommended", and its ranking prefers a Long Term Support Branch (LTSB) over a New Feature Branch (NFB), which on a current GPU is the older branch.
.B oaxaca-drivers-install
instead asks the same library for the candidate packages, keeps the
.B nvidia-driver-<branch>-open
ones that have a
.B linux-modules-nvidia-<branch>-open-<flavour>
package for the installed kernel, takes the highest branch number, and passes it on as
.BR nvidia:<branch>-open .
When no such branch fits (no NVIDIA GPU, or a GPU the open modules do not support, Maxwell to Volta),
.BR ubuntu-drivers '
own default applies: the recommended closed branch, or nothing.
.PP
.B --no-oem
keeps
.B ubuntu-drivers
from adding Canonical's OEM enablement archives to apt's sources.
.B --package-list
appends the installed packages to
.IR /var/log/oaxaca/drivers.list .
Other arguments are passed on to
.BR "ubuntu-drivers install" .
A
.I driver
argument (one that does not start with a dash, such as
.B nvidia:580-open
or
.BR nvidia-driver-580 )
names the driver to install and switches the branch choice off.
.PP
The Oaxaca installer runs this command against the target system. After a GPU change, run it again by hand.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --show
Print the chosen driver and the packages
.B ubuntu-drivers
would install, one line each, and exit without installing. Needs no root.
.SH FILES
.I /var/log/oaxaca/drivers.list
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ubuntu-drivers (8)
